            "heading": "Why \"Without NEET\" Keeps Shifting",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Andhra Pradesh moved its four-year BSc Nursing admission to NEET UG from 2026-27 for government and private colleges, in place of the earlier state test."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "neet-shift",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 6,
            "supporting": [
              "Andhra Pradesh moved its four-year BSc Nursing admission to NEET UG from 2026-27 for government and private colleges, in place of the earlier state test. The NTR University of Health Sciences notification asks applicants to have appeared in NEET UG 2026 and to hold 45 percent in science subjects (40 percent for SC, ST and BC)."
            ]
          },
          {
            "needId": "proof:3",
            "type": "proof",
            "heading": "Starting Pay Is Modest",
            "kind": "items",
            "figures": [],
            "sourceSectionId": "eight-lanes",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 3,
            "supporting": [
              "Starting pay is modest. AmbitionBox lists pharmacists at roughly Rs 1.2 to 4.1 lakh a year across 23,000-plus salary reports (data as of July 2025). Pay climbs when you move into quality, regulatory, research or an owned pharmacy."
            ],
            "items": [
